course: dictionary
lesson: 12333
title: Courteous and polite words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Courteous means polite, kind and showing respect for other people. You can often work it out from the words around it. «The courteous driver waited until we had crossed the road.» Waiting for people to cross is kind and shows respect, so courteous must mean polite and considerate.
explain: Courteous is often used for good manners. «She gave a courteous reply and thanked the visitor for coming.» A reply that thanks someone is polite, so the word fits. Try swapping in polite: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Stories also use courteous for kind, respectful heroes. «The courteous knight bowed before the queen.» A bow is a sign of respect, so a courteous knight is a polite and well-mannered one. The noun is courtesy, which means good manners.
fact: Courteous means polite, kind and showing respect for others.
fact: Courteous is an adjective. You can say more courteous or most courteous.
fact: The noun is courtesy: «She showed courtesy to every visitor.»
fact: Courteous is used for manners and service, as in «a courteous manner» and «courteous service».
exercise: «The courteous shop assistant helped us find the right size.» What does courteous mean? | Cheap | *Polite and kind | Loud and rushed | Very tired
exercise: «The knight made a courteous bow to the princess.» What does a courteous bow show? | Boredom | *Respect | Anger | Hunger
exercise: «Thank you for your courtesy,» said the old man. What is courtesy? | Being rude to people | A loud noise | *Good manners and respect for others | Being in a hurry
test: «Please be courteous to the bus driver when you get on.» Which word means the same as courteous? | Lazy | Rude | *Polite | Silent
test: «The courteous reply made the visitors smile.» Which word means the opposite of courteous? | Polite | Respectful | *Rude | Kind
exam: Which sentence shows courteous behaviour? | «She shouted at the door all afternoon.» | «She slammed the door and ran off.» | *«She held the door open and said thank you.»
